{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>And you shall revere My sanctuary.</b> That one comes to the sanctuary on the three pilgrim festivals. And it is possible that the reason for <i>you shall not make idols for yourselves</i> is because He said <i>they are My servants</i> — and since they are My servants, they shall serve Me alone and not others." "<b>And idol.</b> Known." "<b>And standing-stone.</b> For an idol." "<b>Mashkīt.</b> A noun, like <i>marbīt</i>. Its meaning: a decorated stone, from the root of <i>over him the longings of the heart</i> (Genesis 31:36), <i>desired objects</i> (Numbers 5:21)." "<b>You shall not place in your land.</b> This is the law of idolatry in the form of a Mercurius stone." "<b>For I am YHWH your Elohim.</b> To Me you shall bow down. And so in the Jerusalem Targum." "<b>You shall keep My sabbaths.</b> The years of the sabbatical cycle." "<b>And you shall revere My sanctuary.</b> The year of the Jubilee, for thus it is written <i>it shall be holy to you</i> (Leviticus 25:12). And in my opinion, he mentioned <i>My sabbaths</i> on account of <i>from sabbath to sabbath, all flesh shall come to bow down before Me</i> (Isaiah 66:23), and not because he mentioned bowing down upon it. And the meaning is that you shall come every sabbath to bow down before Me, and not upon a decorated stone — only <i>My sanctuary</i>. Now he mentioned the chosen day, for it is chosen for the service of HaShem, as I explained, and he also mentioned the chosen place." "And the meaning of <b>I am YHWH</b> is that I rested from all work on the sabbath, and My glory dwells in the sanctuary; therefore he mentioned the word <i>you shall revere</i>."], :book :leviticus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:12:40.436723875Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}